    "content": "# Bangkok to Chiang Mai by EV — A 3-Day Family Road Trip Through Northern Thailand\n\nNorthern Thailand is famous for its misty mountains, ancient temples, elephant sanctuaries, and legendary street food. But it's also home to one of Southeast Asia's most scenic EV road trips: the 695 km drive from Bangkok to Chiang Mai.\n\nWith Thailand's EV charging network now exceeding 12,000 public points (2026), the classic Bangkok–Chiang Mai route is fully electrified. The journey takes you through the central plains, sunflower fields of Lopburi, historic Sukhothai, and into the mountainous valleys of Chiang Mai.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- Route is **695 km** via Highway 11 — **2-3 charging stops** depending on range\n- Total charging cost: ~**THB 550-850 ($15-24 USD)** one way — vs THB 2,000+ for petrol\n- Best networks: **PEA Volta** (60-120 kW) and **EA Anywhere** (60-150 kW) along entire route\n- **Estimated time:** 10-12 hours driving + 2-3 hours charging = 3 days recommended\n\n## Route Selection\n\n### Route A: Highway 11 (Recommended)\nBangkok → Saraburi → Phitsanulok → Uttaradit → Lampang → Lamphun → Chiang Mai\n- **695 km** | Chargers every 80-120 km | Divided highway entire route\n\n### Route B: Highway 117/110 (Alternative)\nBangkok → Nakhon Sawan → Phichit → Phitsanulok → Tak → Lampang\n- **680 km** | Fewer chargers between Nakhon Sawan and Tak\n\n**Route A (Highway 11) is the clear winner** — better roads, more chargers, more rest stops.\n\n## Charging Stop Strategy\n\n### Short-Range EV (300-350 km range)\n**Bangkok → Phitsanulok (380 km):** PEA Volta Phitsanulok (120 kW) — 30-40 min\n**Phitsanulok → Lampang (195 km):** EA Anywhere Lampang (150 kW) — 15-20 min\n**Lampang → Chiang Mai (100 km):** Optional top-up at PEA Volta Chiang Mai\n\n### Long-Range EV (500+ km range)\n**Bangkok → Lampang (575 km):** Mid-route top-up at PEA Volta Phitsanulok — 30 min\n**Lampang → Chiang Mai (100 km):** Overnight charge at hotel\n\n## Detailed Charging Stops\n\n### Stop 1: PEA Volta Phitsanulok — The Critical Halfway Point\n**Location:** Highway 11, Km 380, Mueang Phitsanulok\n**Chargers:** 4x CCS2 120 kW DC | **Cost:** THB 6.50/kWh (~THB 325 for 50 kWh)\n**Amenities:** 7-Eleven, food court, clean restrooms, shaded parking\n**Family tip:** **Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat (Wat Yai)** is 10 min away. Free entry, stroller-friendly, kids feed turtles. Spend 30-45 min while charging.\n\n### Stop 2: EA Anywhere Lampang — Mountain Gateway\n**Location:** Central Plaza Lampang | **Chargers:** 4x CCS2 150 kW DC\n**Cost:** THB 7.00/kWh (~THB 175 for 25 kWh)\n**Amenities:** Shopping mall, food court, cinema, indoor kids' play area\n**Family tip:** **Lampang Elephant Conservation Centre** — 30 min east. Elephant bathing shows 9:30 AM and 1:30 PM. THB 100/adult, kids free.\n\n### Stop 3 (Optional): PEA Volta Chiang Mai\n**Location:** Central Festival Chiang Mai | **Chargers:** 6x CCS2 120 kW\n**Amenities:** Massive mall, indoor playground, cinema, trampoline park\n\n### Backup Stations\nSaraburi (PEA Volta 100kW) | Wang Muang (PEA Volta 60kW) | Phichit (EA Anywhere 100kW) | Uttaradit (PEA Volta 60kW) | Den Chai (PEA Volta 100kW)\n\n## 3-Day Family Itinerary\n\n### Day 1: Bangkok → Phitsanulok (380 km)\n\n**Morning (7-11:30 AM):** Depart Bangkok with 100% charge. Exit via Highway 117, avoid 7-9 AM traffic. Quick photo stop at Muak Lek Waterfall (Saraburi, 130 km).\n\n**Lunch & charge (11:30 AM-1 PM):** PEA Volta Phitsanulok. Arrive at ~15-20%. 120 kW charger. Food court (khao soi, pad Thai, THB 60-100). Visit Wat Yai while charging. 30-40 min from 20% to 80%.\n\n**Check-in (1-3 PM):** **Topland Hotel & Convention Centre** — standard outlets for overnight charging.\n\n**Afternoon (3-5 PM):** **Phitsanulok City Park** — playground, pedal boats (THB 50/30 min). **Sgt. Maj. Thawee Folk Museum** (THB 50).\n\n**Evening (5:30-7:30 PM):** **Phitsanulok Night Market** near Wat Yai. Street food: pork skewers (THB 10), som tam (THB 40), mango sticky rice (THB 50).\n\n**Charging tip:** Portable EVSE on standard outlet adds 100-150 km overnight.\n\n### Day 2: Phitsanulok → Lampang → Chiang Mai (295 km)\n\n**Morning (7-9 AM):** Unplug at 100%. Drive 195 km to Lampang.\n\n**Charge & play (9-10:30 AM):** EA Anywhere Central Plaza Lampang — 150 kW. 15 min to 60%. Kids' indoor play area. Second breakfast at food court.\n\n**Mid-morning (10:30 AM-12 PM):** **Lampang Elephant Conservation Centre** — 30 min drive. Elephant bathing shows. THB 100/adult, kids free.\n\n**Drive (12-1:30 PM):** 100 km through scenic mountain passes approaching Doi Suthep.\n\n**Arrival (1:30-3 PM):** **Shangri-La Chiang Mai** (EV charging), **Dhara Dhevi** (EV charging), or **Akyra Manor**.\n\n**Afternoon (3-5 PM):** Old City exploration — Wat Phra Singh, Wat Chedi Luang. **Chiang Mai Night Bazaar** at 6 PM.\n\n**Evening:** **Khao Soi Khun Yai** — best khao soi in town (THB 60/bowl). Night Bazaar stroll.\n\n### Day 3: Explore Chiang Mai and Return\n\n**Morning (7-10 AM):** **Doi Suthep Temple** — 30 min drive. 306-step naga staircase with kids. Entry THB 30 (free for kids).\n\n**Mid-morning (10 AM-12 PM):** **Elephant Jungle Sanctuary** — ethical elephant experience. Half-day ~THB 1,500-2,500/adult. Book on [Klook](https://www.klook.com/activity/).\n\n**Lunch (12:30-1:30 PM):** **Rustic & Blue** — organic farm-to-table, kids' menu.\n\n**Afternoon (1:30-3:30 PM):** **Chiang Mai Zoo & Aquarium** — pandas, penguins, underwater tunnel. THB 150/adult, THB 70/child.\n\n**Departure (3:30-4 PM):** Top up at **Central Festival Chiang Mai** (PEA Volta 120 kW) — 20 min while grabbing snacks for the return.\n\n## Cost Breakdown (3-Day Round Trip, Family of 4)\n\n**Charging:** THB 1,100-1,700 | **Accommodation:** THB 5,000-10,000 | **Meals+Activities:** THB 3,000-5,000 | **Tolls:** THB 600-800\n**Total:** ~$270-490 USD\n\n## Seasonal Tips\n\n- **Best time:** November to February (cool season, clear roads)\n- **Avoid:** Songkran (April 13-15) — chaotic roads, charger queues\n- **Rainy season (Jun-Oct):** Heavy afternoon downpours. Drive slower, charge in mornings.\n\n## 🛒 Book Your EV Trip\n\nReady to plan your own electric road trip? Here are the best tools to get started:\n\n- **🚗 Rent an EV**: Compare prices on [Booking.com Car Rentals](https://www.booking.com/cars.html?aid=2875669)\n- **🏨 Hotels with EV charging**: Book a stay at [Bangkok%2C+Thailand hotels with EV charging on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Bangkok%2C+Thailand&aid=2875669)\n- **🎫 Local activities**: Find tours and attractions on [Klook](https://www.klook.com/?aid=119991)\n\n\n\n👉 [Search EV Charging in Thailand](/search?country=Thailand)\n👉 [Book EV-Friendly Hotels in Chiang Mai](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Chiang+Mai&filter=ev_charging)\n👉 [Chiang Mai Activities on Klook](https://www.klook.com/search?keyword=Chiang+Mai)",
