    "content": "# Hong Kong to Shenzhen Electric Road Trip — Family-Friendly EV Itinerary\n\nHong Kong and Shenzhen — two of the most dynamic cities in Asia, separated by just 30 km of water and connected by a handful of bridges and tunnels. Driving an EV between them in 2026 is not just possible; it's the smartest way for a family to explore the Greater Bay Area. With Shenzhen's world-class charging infrastructure and Hong Kong's growing network, a cross-border EV road trip is a perfect weekend adventure.\n\nThis guide covers everything: what you need for cross-border driving, charging stations in both cities, family-friendly activities at each stop, and how to make the most of your electric weekend.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- The Hong Kong–Shenzhen journey is **30-45 minutes** driving (excluding border crossing time) — among the shortest international EV road trips in Asia\n- Total charging cost for a weekend: approximately **HKD 200-350 ($26-45 USD)** — compared to HKD 600+ for petrol\n- **Shenzhen has over 160,000 public charging points** — one of the densest EV networks in the world\n- Hong Kong EV charging is improving: **CLP and Shell Recharge** now operate 60+ fast-charging stations across the city\n- **Estimated driving + charging time for a weekend:** 4-6 hours total (including border processing)\n\n## Cross-Border Requirements\n\n### What You Need to Drive from Hong Kong to Shenzhen\n\n**Hong Kong vehicle license + cross-border permit:** Your HK-registered EV needs a Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macau vehicle permit. Cost: HKD 4,000-6,000 (one-time) + annual fee.\n\n**Chinese temporary driver's license:** ~RMB 50 at Vehicle Management Office near Huanggang or Shenzhen Bay Port.\n\n**Chinese insurance:** Minimum third-party liability, ~RMB 1,000/year.\n\n**GB/T adapter:** Hong Kong uses CCS2/Type 2; mainland uses GB/T. HKD 800-1,500.\n\n**ETC tag:** For expressway tolls in Guangdong.\n\n> **Important:** Cross-border permits have a quota — 8-12 week wait. No permit? Park at HK border and take the MTR across.\n\n### Easier Alternative: Rent an EV on the Mainland Side\n\n1. Take MTR from Hong Kong to **Shenzhen Futian Station** (14 min from Admiralty)\n2. Rent an EV from Shenzhou or eHi — ~**RMB 200-400/day**\n3. Already has GB/T, green plate, and insurance\n\n## EV Charging in Hong Kong\n\n**CLP Power:** 40+ stations, 50-120 kW DC, HKD 3.50/kWh\n**Shell Recharge:** 20+ stations, 60-150 kW DC, HKD 3.80/kWh\n**Tesla Supercharger:** 8 stations (200+ stalls), up to 250 kW, free for Tesla\n**HK Electric:** Hong Kong Island + Lantau, 50-100 kW DC, HKD 3.20/kWh\n\n**Best pre-crossing charge:** CLP Mega Box in Kowloon Bay — 8x CCS2 120 kW, ice skating, playground.\n\n### Top Family-Friendly Charging Spots in HK\n\n**Kowloon Bay — Mega Box (CLP 120kW):** 8x CCS2, ice skating, playground, cinema\n**Tsing Yi — Maritime Square (Shell 150kW):** 4x CCS2, mall, Tsing Yi Park playground\n**Shatin — New Town Plaza (CLP 100kW):** 6x CCS2, indoor play areas, Snoopy's World\n**Tuen Mun Town Plaza (HK Electric 60kW):** 4x CCS2, beach, ferry pier\n**Ocean Park (CLP 50kW):** 2x CCS2, Ocean Park theme park with pandas\n\n## EV Charging in Shenzhen\n\nShenzhen — **EV charging capital of the world** (100% electric public transit since 2017).\n\n**TELD:** 3,000+ stations, 60-180 kW DC, RMB 0.80-1.50/kWh\n**Star Charge:** 2,500+ stations, 60-120 kW DC, RMB 0.70-1.20/kWh\n**BYD:** 1,000+ stations, 60-120 kW DC, RMB 0.60-1.00/kWh\n**State Grid:** 500+ stations, 60-180 kW DC, RMB 0.90-1.30/kWh\n\n### Best Family-Friendly Charging Spots in Shenzhen\n\n**KK Mall — Luohu:** TELD 120kW, 8 slots. Indoor playground, 500m from border.\n**MixC World — Nanshan:** Star Charge 120kW, 12 slots. Largest mall, indoor playland.\n**COCO Park — Futian:** TELD 120kW, 6 slots. Outdoor kids' play area, cinema.\n**OCT Bay — Nanshan:** Star Charge 60kW, 8 slots. Waterfront dining, aquarium.\n**Shenzhen Safari Park:** TELD 120kW, 6 slots. Zoo — charge while you explore.\n**Window of the World:** State Grid 120kW, 10 slots. Miniature landmarks theme park.\n**Shenzhen Bay Park:** Star Charge 60kW, 4 slots. 15 km coastal promenade, bikes.\n\n## Weekend Itinerary: Hong Kong to Shenzhen to Hong Kong\n\n### Day 1: Hong Kong Departure to Shenzhen Arrival\n\n**Morning (7-9 AM):** Depart HK hotel. Battery 80%+. Use **Shenzhen Bay Port**. Toll: HKD 50 bridge + RMB 20 expressway.\n\n**Border crossing (9-10:30 AM):** 30-60 min at Shenzhen Bay Port. Leave before 8 AM.\n\n**Arrival charge (10:30-11:30 AM):** Haiya Mega Mall, 5 min from port. TELD 120kW. 25-35 min. ~RMB 30-50.\n\n**Late morning (11:30 AM-1 PM):** Shenzhen Bay Park — free entry, kids run on grass. Bike rental RMB 40/hr.\n\n**Lunch (1-2:30 PM):** OCT Bay — Haidilao hotpot with kids' playroom. Charge at Star Charge 60kW while dining.\n\n**Afternoon (2:30-5:30 PM):** Shenzhen Children's Palace — planetarium, earthquake simulator, hands-on science. Free entry.\n\n**Evening (5:30-8 PM):** MixC World — dinner at Food Street (B1). Kids' play area 3rd floor. Charge at Star Charge 120kW while shopping.\n\n**Overnight:** Ritz-Carlton Shenzhen or InterContinental Shenzhen. Both have EV charging. Filter [Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Shenzhen&filter=ev_charging).\n\n### Day 2: Explore Shenzhen and Return to HK\n\n**Morning (8-10 AM):** Unplug at 100%. Drive 25 min to **Shenzhen Safari Park** — pandas, elephants. Book on [Klook](https://www.klook.com/activity/). Charge at TELD 120kW.\n\n**Lunch (12:30-1:30 PM):** Panda Restaurant at zoo.\n\n**Afternoon (1:30-4 PM):** **Window of the World** — miniature landmarks. Tickets RMB 220/adult. Book on Klook.\n\n**Late afternoon (4-5:30 PM):** **Dongmen Pedestrian Street** — street food: bubble tea, grilled squid. Kids' arcade Dongmen Mall.\n\n**Evening (5:30-7:30 PM):** Top up at TELD KK Mall (Luohu). 5 min from Lo Wu checkpoint. Dinner 5th floor kids' dining zone.\n\n**Return (7:30-9 PM):** Lo Wu/Luohu Port (open until 12 AM). 30-60 min customs.\n\n## Cost Breakdown (Weekend, Family of 4)\n\n**Charging:** HKD 160-270 | **Tolls:** HKD 80-100 | **Meals:** HKD 600-1,000\n**Attractions:** HKD 600-800 | **Hotel:** HKD 800-1,500 | **Total:** ~$290-470 USD\n\n## Pro Tips\n\n**HK-Side:** Charge to 100% night before. Download WeChat and Alipay. Buy China SIM at Lo Wu.\n\n**Driving in SZ:** Use Baidu Maps or Amap. Green plate = free parking + bus lane access.\n\n**Border:** Shenzhen Bay Port 6:30 AM-12 AM. Huanggang 24h. Lo Wu 6 AM-12 AM. Avoid Fri ev/Mon morning.\n\n## 🛒 Book Your EV Trip\n\nReady to plan your own electric road trip? Here are the best tools to get started:\n\n- **🚗 Rent an EV**: Compare prices on [Booking.com Car Rentals](https://www.booking.com/cars.html?aid=2875669)\n- **🏨 Hotels with EV charging**: Book a stay at [Shenzhen%2C+China hotels with EV charging on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Shenzhen%2C+China&aid=2875669)\n- **🎫 Local activities**: Find tours and attractions on [Klook](https://www.klook.com/?aid=119991)\n\n\n\n👉 [Search EV Charging in Hong Kong](/search?country=Hong+Kong)\n👉 [Book EV-Friendly Hotels in Shenzhen](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Shenzhen&filter=ev_charging)\n👉 [Shenzhen Activities on Klook](https://www.klook.com/search?keyword=Shenzhen)",
    "imageUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558979158-65a1eaa08691?w=1200",
